# Copy to .build-secrets.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Used by `npm run
# build:ios:testflight`, `release:ios:testflight` and `submit:ios:testflight`.
#
# Where the App Store Connect API key (.p8) lives on THIS machine:
EXPO_ASC_API_KEY_PATH=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
# The key's id and the issuer id, both shown on App Store Connect > Users and Access > Integrations:
EXPO_ASC_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
EXPO_ASC_ISSUER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# Your Apple Developer team id (10 characters, shown in the EAS build credentials
# summary and on developer.apple.com > Membership). EAS refuses to use the key
# without it ("App Store Connect credentials are incomplete").
EXPO_APPLE_TEAM_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
#
# Deliberately NOT named ".env.*": Expo treats every .env.* file in the project as
# one of its own environment files and Metro then tries to read it as code.
